<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 144,268 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 144,268 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 144,268 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Friday compared to 65,657 tonnes in the same period on Thursday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Friday	March 6</p>
<p>    Export cargo		29,302	16,438</p>
<p>    Import cargo	     114,966	49,219</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and seven berthed. In the next 24 hours, 10 are expected to sail and 11 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 60,000	 Miraj		   7/3</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasen Megah	 7/3</p>
<p>High speed diesel    55,660	 Warbah		  7/3</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     22,649	 Seram		   9/3</p>
<p>Phosphate		29,887	 Lapanto Glory	20/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
